sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-girardia-14> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Partial, variable gap-junction blockade is consistent with stochastic head-shape outcomes" ;
    dct:description "The variability and overall magnitude of the bioelectric effect imply that octanol only partially shuts down gap junction communication in each G. dorotocephala (affecting some percentage of gap junctions per animal), which the authors consider consistent with the stochasticity of the head-shape phenotype." ;
    delphi:context "Emmons-Bell M, Durant F, Hammelman J, Bessonov N, Volpert V, Morokuma J, Pinet K, Adams DS, Pietak A, Lobo D, Levin M, “Gap Junctional Blockade Stochastically Induces Different Species-Specific Head Anatomies in Genetically Wild-Type Girardia dorotocephala Flatworms”, International journal of molecular sciences (2015), doi:10.3390/ijms161126065; section “3. Discussion › 3.4. Bioelectric State of Tissues and Its Stable Alteration in Species-Specific Shape Change”. Scope: Octanol-treated G. dorotocephala" ;
    dct:type "mechanism" .
}

